Sure macha 😎 Here’s the Vector difference in C++, Java, and Python.

| **Feature**               | **C++ `vector`**         | **Java `ArrayList`**                        | **Python `list`**      |
| ------------------------- | ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------- | ---------------------- |
| **Name**                  | `vector`                 | `ArrayList`                                 | `list`                 |
| **Import**                | `#include <vector>`      | `import java.util.ArrayList;`               | No import              |
| **Declaration**           | `vector<int> v;`         | `ArrayList<Integer> v = new ArrayList<>();` | `v = []`               |
| **Type**                  | Dynamic array            | Dynamic array                               | Dynamic, flexible list |
| **Add at Back**           | `v.push_back(10)`        | `v.add(10)`                                 | `v.append(10)`         |
| **Access by Index**       | `v[0]`                   | `v.get(0)`                                  | `v[0]`                 |
| **Update by Index**       | `v[0] = 50`              | `v.set(0, 50)`                              | `v[0] = 50`            |
| **Size**                  | `v.size()`               | `v.size()`                                  | `len(v)`               |
| **Remove Last**           | `v.pop_back()`           | `v.remove(v.size() - 1)`                    | `v.pop()`              |
| **Remove by Index**       | `v.erase(v.begin() + i)` | `v.remove(i)`                               | `v.pop(i)`             |
| **Clear**                 | `v.clear()`              | `v.clear()`                                 | `v.clear()`            |
| **Empty Check**           | `v.empty()`              | `v.isEmpty()`                               | `not v`                |
| **First Element**         | `v.front()`              | `v.get(0)`                                  | `v[0]`                 |
| **Last Element**          | `v.back()`               | `v.get(v.size()-1)`                         | `v[-1]`                |
| **Can Store Primitives?** | ✅ Yes                    | ❌ Uses wrapper types like `Integer`         | ✅ Yes                  |
| **Type Safety**           | Strong                   | Strong                                      | Dynamic typing         |
| **Random Access**         | O(1)                     | O(1)                                        | O(1)                   |
| **Add at Back**           | O(1) amortized           | O(1) amortized                              | O(1) amortized         |
| **Insert Middle**         | O(n)                     | O(n)                                        | O(n)                   |
| **Remove Middle**         | O(n)                     | O(n)                                        | O(n)                   |



METHOD NAME DIFFERENACE 

| **Operation**    | **C++**          | **Java**                                    | **Python** |
| ---------------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------------------- | ---------- |
| **Create**       | `vector<int> v;` | `ArrayList<Integer> v = new ArrayList<>();` | `v = []`   |
| **Add**          | `push_back()`    | `add()`                                     | `append()` |
| **Access**       | `v[i]`           | `v.get(i)`                                  | `v[i]`     |
| **Update**       | `v[i] = x`       | `v.set(i, x)`                               | `v[i] = x` |
| **Remove Last**  | `pop_back()`     | `remove(size()-1)`                          | `pop()`    |
| **Remove Index** | `erase()`        | `remove(i)`                                 | `pop(i)`   |
| **Size**         | `size()`         | `size()`                                    | `len()`    |
| **Clear**        | `clear()`        | `clear()`                                   | `clear()`  |
| **Empty**        | `empty()`        | `isEmpty()`                                 | `not v`    |
| **First**        | `front()`        | `get(0)`                                    | `v[0]`     |
| **Last**         | `back()`         | `get(size()-1)`                             | `v[-1]`    |


